# Pictures by name (#128): two characters rolled from the gallery's Character creator pictures, each with all its views, meet in one clip. Orrery Refs loads their pictures itself, no Load Image needed; the language model writes who they are from the prompts that made them.
# Workflow: orrery_h3_ref2va (Orrery Prompt picks → Orrery Refs → Reference to Video). Try: a seed per pair · __pictures/krea/09_character_creator[loved]__ for the ones you loved · a name from the Libraries tab (image krea/09_character_creator/SEED) to pin one.
@h3 references 16:9 0.6MP
style: live-action, warm evening light in a roadside diner, photorealistic, handheld, shallow depth of field

CAST
@HERO (image __pictures/krea/09_character_creator__): --who they are, in one sentence--
@STRANGER (image __pictures/krea/09_character_creator__): --who they are, in one sentence--
keep: face, outfit

SHOT 3s: static, medium
@HERO stirs a cup of coffee in a red vinyl booth, rain running down the window behind.
SFX: rain on the glass, a spoon against a mug, a fridge humming

SHOT 3s: push in, small, slow
@STRANGER slides into the seat across and sets a key on the table between them.
@STRANGER (low, calm): You kept it.
SFX: vinyl creaking, the key clicking on formica
